      "[Java / C++ / C / JavaScript / C#] %100 easy to understand zeldox 1332 53765 Nov 29, 2020 Java C JavaScript if you like it pls upvote \n Java \n class   Solution   { \n      public   int   maximumWealth ( int [ ] [ ]  accounts )   { \n          int  res  =   0 ; \n          for ( int  i  = 0 ; i < accounts . length ; i ++ ) { \n              int  temp  =   0 ; \n              for ( int  j  =   0 ; j < accounts [ i ] . length ; j ++ ) { \n                 temp += accounts [ i ] [ j ] ; \n              } \n             res  =  Math . max ( res , temp ) ; \n          } \n          return  res ; \n      } \n } \n C++ \n class   Solution   { \n public : \n      int   maximumWealth ( vector < vector < int >> &  accounts )   { \n          int  res  =   0 ; \n          for ( int  i  = 0 ; i < accounts . size ( ) ; i ++ ) { \n              int  temp  =   0 ; \n              for ( int  j  =   0 ; j < accounts [ i ] . size ( ) ; j ++ ) { \n                 temp += accounts [ i ] [ j ] ; \n              } \n             res  =   max ( res , temp ) ; \n          } \n          return  res ; \n      } \n } ; \n C \n int   maximumWealth ( int * *  accounts ,   int  accountsSize ,   int *  accountsColSize ) { \n          int  res  =   0 ; \n          for ( int  i  = 0 ; i < accountsSize ; i ++ ) { \n              int  temp  =   0 ; \n              for ( int  j  =   0 ; j < * accountsColSize ; j ++ ) { \n                 temp += accounts [ i ] [ j ] ; \n              } \n              if ( temp  >  res )  res  =  temp ; \n          } \n          return  res ; \n } \n JavaScript \n var   maximumWealth   =   function ( accounts )   { \n          var  res  =   0 ; \n          for ( var  i  = 0 ; i < accounts . length ; i ++ ) { \n              var  temp  =   0 ; \n              for ( var  j  =   0 ; j < accounts [ i ] . length ; j ++ ) { \n                 temp += accounts [ i ] [ j ] ; \n              } \n             res  =   Math . max ( res , temp ) ; \n          } \n          return  res ; \n } ; \n C# \n public   class   Solution   { \n      public   int   MaximumWealth ( int [ ] [ ]  accounts )   { \n          int  res  =   0 ; \n          for ( int  i  = 0 ; i < accounts . Length ; i ++ ) { \n              int  temp  =   0 ; \n              for ( int  j  =   0 ; j < accounts [ i ] . Length ; j ++ ) { \n                 temp += accounts [ i ] [ j ] ; \n              } \n             res  =  Math . Max ( res , temp ) ; \n          } \n          return  res ; \n      } \n } Comments (26) coderaky Jan 30, 2022 45 Show 4 Replies Reply zheyujie Jan 30, 2022 17 Reply oregon_blazer Mar 06, 2021 For java, you might want to use stream to sum up wealth in all accounts: \n \npublic int maximumWealth(int[][] accounts) { \nint maxWealth = Integer.MIN_VALUE; \nfor (int[] account : accounts) { \nmaxWealth = Math.max(maxWealth, Arrays.stream(account).sum()); \n} \nreturn maxWealth; \n} \n Read more 21 Show 5 Replies Reply dev_amit Jul 18, 2022 Read more 5 Reply user9904J May 25, 2021 Read more 9 Show 4 Replies Reply user5975n Oct 15, 2023 Very slow solution with included loops 1 Reply imankhaledaz Jan 13, 2023 why is there the '&' symbol in between the vector name and its type declaration? 1 Show 1 Replies Reply isleetcode Jun 28, 2021 compared with lee215's one liner, i like your method better in terms of readability. 1 Show 1 Replies Reply ABHAY_RAI Jan 05, 2021 best 1 Show 2 Replies Reply dshelem Feb 08, 2021 For C++ you should use STL algorithms (here, std::accumulate) whenever it's possible. They are heavily optimized. 1 Show 1 Replies Reply",
      "[Python , Javascript]  Easy solution with Explanation mageshyt 4049 6349 Jan 30, 2022 Python JavaScript <img src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/users/images/45273f37-1a1c-4a31-bc1e-7c1fc7b032c2_1643603719.42253.png\" alt=\"image\"> \n You  are given an m x n integer grid accounts  where  accounts [ i ] [ j ]  is the amount of money  [ i ]  customer  customer has  in  their bank . \n      Example : \n     accounts  =   [ [ 2 , 8 , 7 ] , [ 7 , 1 , 3 ] , [ 1 , 9 , 5 ] ] \n          Here \n             👨🏻‍💻  [ 2 , 8 , 7 ]   - ->  person  1  amount  in  there respective banks\n            🧑🏻‍💼  [ 7 , 1 , 3 ]   - ->  person  2  amount  in  there respective banks\n            🕵🏻‍♂️  [ 1 , 9 , 5 ]   - ->  person  3  amount  in  there respective banks\n          Now  we need to find the total  in  the   [ i ]  customer 's  bank . \n          The  total money that the  [ 1 ]  customer has : \n              2   +   8   +   7   =   17 \n          The  total money that the  [ 2 ]  customer has : \n              7   +   1   +   3   =   11 \n          The  total money that the  [ 3 ]  customer has  : \n              1   +   9   +   5   =   15 \n      Now  we need  return  the wealthy customer amount\n          From  the given data person  [ 1 ]  👨🏻‍💻 is the most rich 🤑 . \n         so we need to  return   17 \n \t\t\n      Big   O   : \n         m  - ->  customer\n         n  - ->  bank\n          Time : O ( m * n )  \n          Space : O ( 1 ) \n \n Solution : \n \n \n Python: \n \t\t class   Solution : \n      def   maximumWealth ( self ,   accounts :  List [ List [ int ] ] )   - >  int : \n         wealthy_person = 0 \n          for  balance  in  accounts : \n             total = sum ( balance ) \n             wealthy_person = max ( wealthy_person , total ) \n          return  wealthy_person \n Javascript: \n //! function to find the sum of array \n const   sum   =   ( arr )   =>   { \n    let  sum  =   0 ; \n    for   ( let  i  =   0 ;  i  <  arr . length ;  i ++ )   { \n     sum  +=  arr [ i ] ; \n    } \n    return  sum ; \n } ; \n \n const   maximumWealth   =   ( accounts )   =>   { \n    let  wealthy_customer  =   0 ; \n    for   ( let  balance  of  accounts )   { \n      const  curr_wealth  =   sum ( balance ) ;   // we will get total balance of the person \n     wealthy_customer  =   Math . max ( wealthy_customer ,  curr_wealth ) ; \n    } \n    return  wealthy_customer ; \n } ; \n UPVOTE if you like 😄 , If you have any question, feel free to ask. Comments (5) Prerna_pundir Jan 31, 2022 Read more 16 Show 2 Replies Reply hi-malik Jan 30, 2022 Wow, that's an Awesome work buddy! \n UpVoted!! 4 Show 3 Replies Reply KondalDurgam Aug 30, 2023 Upvoted😄😄😄 0 Reply gibrianvargas Jan 24, 2023 great explanation! 0 Reply DakuwoN Sep 01, 2022 beautiful job, thank you so much 0 Reply",
      "Javascript 1 line solution cool-void-zero 89 2300 Jan 25, 2021 JavaScript return   Math . max ( ... accounts . map ( customer => customer . reduce ( ( a , b ) => a + b ) ) ) ; Comments (3) bikarajsingha Nov 14, 2021 good stuff 3 Reply ibnulferdous Jan 17, 2023 Great solution! 1 Reply sasegovia Sep 19, 2022 damn nice 1 Reply",
      "Clean JavaScript Solution shimphillip 254 3354 Jan 03, 2021 JavaScript // time O(n^2) space O(n) \n var   maximumWealth   =   function ( accounts )   { \n      return   Math . max ( ... accounts . map ( account   =>  \n         account . reduce ( ( accumulator ,  current )   =>  accumulator  +  current ,   0 ) \n      ) ) \n } ; Comments (9) KristinaA Jan 21, 2021 Read more 12 Show 1 Replies Reply jr4578 Jan 03, 2021 Wow thank you for this, I had this vaguely visualized in my head, but just could not figure out how to implement it. 3 Reply liebsterkamerad Jan 05, 2021 very good 1 Reply tajmirul Nov 02, 2022 I think the time complexity is O(n^3). Because Math.max() function is O(n) complexity. 0 Reply ulanLeet Dec 17, 2021 Read more 0 Show 2 Replies Reply ashi3377 Jun 19, 2021 my answer was also somewhat similar \n var maximumWealth = function (accounts) { \nreturn Math.max(... \naccounts.splice(\",\").map((element) => element.reduce((x, y) => x + y)) \n); \n}; 0 Reply denik1981 Jun 02, 2021 This is not O(n^2). This is O(n^2.log n) if we assume that the implementation of Math.max() is O(log n) and we accept this is a square matrix of #(customers) = #(banks). \nThis is because for each customer in the array (Nc) you then sum up their total wealth on each bank (Nj) and after that you serialize the final result and find the maximum with Math.max which adds a O(log N) extra time. I took a similar approach but I take the advantage of using the Array.reduce to always store the maximum value that I was obtaining at each step. You are also adding up O(n) by creating a new copy of the entire array with  Array.map by usig this method. 0 Show 1 Replies Reply SDAR30 Apr 12, 2021 Is map creating the array and why it is O(n) space? 0 Show 2 Replies Reply appsplash99 Jan 14, 2021 can anyone please explain how is this has time complexity - O(n) 0 Show 5 Replies Reply",
      "fun javascript one liner chazkondo 82 3210 Jan 10, 2023 JavaScript Code \n  \n var   maximumWealth   =   ac   =>  ac . reduce ( ( a ,  b )   =>   Math . max ( a ,  b . reduce ( ( a ,  b )   =>  a  +  b ) ) ,   0 ) Comments (5) lemondaki Aug 19, 2023 clearer way : \nvar maximumWealth = function(accounts) { \nreturn Math.max(...accounts.map(account => account.reduce((money,acc) => money + acc))); \n}; 2 Show 2 Replies Reply shivani28 Aug 02, 2023 woah ! totally not there ! but hopefully will get to one liners and arrow functions soon ! 1 Reply juanelprogrammer Jun 01, 2023 gotta practice that Math.max method! 1 Reply sohodoll Mar 16, 2023 Smart! 1 Reply gulsenkeskin Jan 11, 2023 woowww 1 Reply"
